{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/955976-note-taking-programs","id":955976,"title":"Note-taking Programs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-22T16:32:50-07:00","id":955976,"title":"Note-taking Programs","content":"So I usually used Evernote to organise my gaming notes - the tag system worked really well so that I could pull up whatever collection I wanted, usually in a small enough number I could go through it by hand. But apparently they're limiting access to 2 devices unless you pay for a subscription, which I don't want to do, so I'm looking for alternatives. I've done my googling, but none of the ones recommended have the ease of organisation. Google Docs was appealing, but has little way of organising everything the way I'd like. One Note was possible, but I can see it getting unwieldy when I have a large number - also, maybe I want to pull up all my Hunter: the Reckoning story idea notes, and OneNote doesn't seem to do that.<br /> <br /> So what do you guys use?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:32:17-07:00","id":956592,"title":"","content":"Checkout Google Keep. It's Google's Evernote competitor, it has the label feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divi